  "summaries": {
    "en": "Azur Lane guide—fleet formation, retrofitting priority, and oil cost management for daily farming.",
    "ja": "アズールレーン攻略。艦隊編成・近代化改修優先度・デイリー農場のオイルコスト管理を解説。"
  },
  "category": "strategy",
  "difficulty": "beginner",
  "thumbnail": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1569346028671-efab0e1bcfec?q=80&w=1200&auto=format&fit=crop",
  "keyPoints": {
    "en": [
      "Fleet composition divides into Vanguard (3 ships) and Main Fleet (3 ships); Vanguard is player-controlled, Main Fleet fires automatically—designing both halves independently optimizes fleet performance.",
      "The Retrofit system upgrades older ships with new stats and often new abilities; retrofitting META ships (Essex, Hatsuharu, etc.) provides competitive performance comparable to newer SSR ships at minimal gem cost.",
      "Anti-air (AA) stat management prevents enemy aircraft from reaching your Main Fleet; Vanguard ships with high AA ratings absorb air damage before it reaches the more fragile Main Fleet battleships.",
      "Limit Breaking ships via duplicates or dedicated Break items increases their stat ceiling dramatically; prioritize Limit Breaking your most-used main DPS ships before investing in Fleet composition diversity.",
      "Oil cost per sortie scales with ship level and rarity; low-level Level 1–60 ships consume less oil than max-level ships—maintaining a dedicated \"farming fleet\" of lower-level ships reduces daily oil expenditure by 30–40%."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "艦隊構成は前衛（3隻）と主力艦隊（3隻）に分かれる。前衛はプレイヤー操作、主力艦隊は自動射撃。両方を独立して設計することで艦隊パフォーマンスが最適化される。",
      "近代化改修システムは古い艦艇を新しいステータスと多くの場合新しい能力でアップグレードする。META艦艇（エセックス・初春等）の改修は最小限のジェムコストで新SSR艦艇に匹敵する競争力のあるパフォーマンスを提供する。",
      "対空（AA）ステータス管理は敵の航空機が主力艦隊に到達するのを防ぐ。高いAA評価を持つ前衛艦艇は、より脆弱な主力艦隊の戦艦に到達する前に航空ダメージを吸収する。",
      "複製または専用ブレイクアイテムを通じて艦艇を限界突破するとステータス上限が劇的に増加する。艦隊構成の多様性への投資より最も使用する主力DPS艦艇の限界突破を優先する。",
      "出撃ごとのオイルコストは艦艇レベルとレアリティでスケールする。低レベル1〜60の艦艇は最大レベルの艦艇よりオイルを消費しない。低レベル艦艇の専用「農場艦隊」を維持すると毎日のオイル消費を30〜40%削減する。"
    ]
  },
  "opening": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Building Your First Fleet",
        "body": "The most accessible starting fleets use N (Normal) and R (Rare) rarity ships to minimize oil cost while learning mechanics. A 3-Destroyer Vanguard (high speed, low HP) paired with a 2-Battleship + 1-Carrier Main Fleet provides solid story mode coverage through the first 4 worlds. Enable auto-battle for repetitive grinding stages; reserve manual control for Boss nodes and Elite stages that require dodging special attacks."
      }
    ]
  },
  "midGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Retrofit Priority and Research",
        "body": "The Research Lab (unlocked at Level 60) provides the most powerful equipment blueprints in the game through the PR Ship construction system. Prioritize completing daily Research tasks for PR points; the first Priority Ship (Bismarck or Azuma) requires months of consistent Research investment. Retrofit Priority for story content: Phoenix (damage reduction aura) and Sandy (Firepower aura) are among the highest-impact retrofits for fleet-wide support."
      }
    ]
  },
  "endGame": {
    "en": [
      {
        "title": "Operation Siren and META Showdown",
        "body": "Operation Siren is a permanent open-world event requiring Level 100+ fleets for the harder node encounters. META Showdowns are limited events that pit player fleets against powerful META enemies; defeating these enemies provides META ship fragments for unlocking unique ships not available on the gacha. META Showdown damage is cumulative across all participating commanders, making consistent daily participation more important than single high-damage runs."
      }
    ]
  },
  "mistakes": {
    "en": [
      "Not building a dedicated farming fleet—using your highest-power fleet for all stages burns oil rapidly; a separate 50–70 level fleet completes standard farming stages at 50% oil cost.",
      "Ignoring equipment rarity for DPS ships—equipment rarity directly multiplies base weapon stats; T1 (Gold) equipment on DPS ships provides 2–3x more damage than T3 (Blue) equivalents at the same ship level.",
      "Not participating in monthly Construction rotation banners—Construction banners feature ships not available in standard Construction; missing rotation banners permanently locks those ships until their next banner appearance.",
      "Spending gems on fuel and repairs instead of Dock slots—fuel and repairs are free-farmable resources; Dock expansion (more ship storage slots) is the highest-value permanent gem investment in the early game.",
      "Raising all ships to max level before focusing a core fleet—resource dilution from leveling 30+ ships prevents any single fleet from reaching competitive power levels; concentrate on 6–9 ships for your primary fleet before diversifying."
    ],
    "ja": [
      "専用農場艦隊を構築しない。全ステージで最高パワー艦隊を使うとオイルが急速に消耗する。別の50〜70レベルの艦隊は50%のオイルコストで標準農場ステージを完了する。",
      "DPS艦艇の装備レアリティを無視する。装備レアリティはベース武器ステータスに直接乗算する。DPS艦艇のT1（ゴールド）装備は同じ艦艇レベルのT3（ブルー）の同等品より2〜3倍多くのダメージを提供する。",
      "月次建造ローテーションバナーに参加しない。建造バナーは標準建造では入手できない艦艇を特集する。ローテーションバナーを逃すと次のバナー外観まで永久にそれらの艦艇がロックされる。",
      "燃料と修理の代わりにドックスロットにジェムを使わない。燃料と修理は無料で農場可能なリソース。ドック拡張（より多くの艦艇収納スロット）は序盤ゲームで最高価値の永続ジェム投資。",
      "コア艦隊に集中する前に全ての艦艇を最大レベルに引き上げる。30以上の艦艇をレベルアップすることによるリソース希薄化は競争力のあるパワーレベルに達する単一艦隊を妨げる。多様化する前にメイン艦隊の6〜9隻に集中する。"
    ]
  },
